{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MAT",
  "chapter": 25,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then shall the kingdom of heaven be likened to ten virgins, who took their lamps, and went forth to meet the bridegroom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And five of them were wise, and five ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " foolish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " foolish took their lamps, and took no oil with them:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the wise took oil in their vessels with their lamps.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "While the bridegroom tarried, they all slumbered and slept.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And at midnight there was a cry made, Behold, the bridegroom cometh; go ye out to meet him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then all those virgins arose, and trimmed their lamps.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the foolish said to the wise, Give us of your oil: for our lamps are gone out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the wise answered, saying, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Not so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; lest there be not enough for us and you: but go ye rather to them that sell, and buy for yourselves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And while they were going to buy, the bridegroom came; and they that were ready, went in with him to the marriage, and the door was shut.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Afterward came also the other virgins, saying, Lord, Lord, open to us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he answered and said, Verily I say to you, I know you not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Watch therefore, for ye know neither the day nor the hour in which the Son of man cometh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the kingdom of heaven is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as a man traveling into a far country, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " called his own servants, and delivered to them his goods.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And to one he gave five talents, to another two, and to another one; to every man according to his several ability; and forthwith took his journey.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then he that had received the five talents, went and traded with the same, and gained other five talents.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And likewise he that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "had received",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " two, he also gained other two.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he that had received one, went and digged in the earth, and hid his lord's money.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After a long time the lord of those servants cometh, and reckoneth with them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he that had received five talents, came and brought other five talents, saying, Lord, thou deliveredst to me five talents: behold, I have gained besides them five talents more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His lord said to him, Well done ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thou",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good and faithful servant; thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He also that had received two talents came, and said, Lord, thou deliveredst to me two talents: behold, I have gained two other talents besides them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His lord said to him, Well done, good and faithful servant; thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then he who had received the one talent came, and said, Lord, I knew thee that thou art a hard man, reaping where thou hast not sown, and gathering where thou hast not strewed:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I was afraid, and went and hid thy talent in the earth: lo, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "what is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His lord answered and said to him, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Thou",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wicked and slothful servant, thou knewest that I reap where I have not sown, and gather where I have not strewed:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou oughtest therefore to have put my money to the exchangers, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "then",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " at my coming I should have received my own with interest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take therefore the talent from him, and give ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to him who hath ten talents.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For to every one that hath shall be given, and he shall have abundance: but from him that hath not shall be taken away even that which he hath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And cast ye the unprofitable servant into utter darkness: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the Son of man shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then will he sit upon the throne of his glory:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And before him shall be gathered all nations: and he will separate them one from another, as a shepherd divideth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sheep from the goats:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he will set the sheep on his right hand, but the goats on the left.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then will the King say to them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I was hungry, and ye gave me food: I was thirsty, and ye gave me drink: I was a stranger, and ye took me in:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Naked, and ye clothed me: I was sick, and ye visited me: I was in prison, and ye came to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then will the righteous answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee hungry, and fed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? or thirsty, and gave ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " drink?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When saw we thee a stranger, and took ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in? or naked, and clothed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or when saw we thee sick, or in prison, and came to thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the king will answer and say to them, Verily I say to you, Inasmuch as ye have done ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then will he say also to them on the left hand, Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I was hungry, and ye gave me no food: I was thirsty, and ye gave me no drink:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was a stranger, and ye took me not in: naked, and ye clothed me not: sick, and in prison, and ye visited me not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then will they also answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee hungry, or thirsty, or a stranger, or naked, or sick, or in prison, and did not minister to thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then will he answer them, saying, Verily I say to you, Inasmuch as ye did ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not to one of the least of these, ye did ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.25.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.25.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And these shall go away into everlasting punishment: but the righteous into life eternal.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
